# =============================================================================
# Case D : multi-component (vector) magnetic field  (TRUST-LiMe standalone MHD)
# =============================================================================
#  Exercises the DEFAULT component count (nb_composantes omitted -> dimension)
#  and that the components are treated as INDEPENDENT scalar fields (the field
#  nature is multi_scalaire) each solving its own diffusion problem.
#
#  In 2D the unknown has two components b = (bx, by). On the unit square with
#  homogeneous Dirichlet conditions on all four faces, the Laplacian eigenmodes
#  are  sin(m pi x) sin(n pi y)  with decay rate  eta (m^2 + n^2) pi^2.
#  We give the two components DIFFERENT modes so that their decay rates differ;
#  any component swap or mixed assembly is then caught by the probes:
#
#      bx(x,y,t) = sin(pi x) sin(pi y) exp(-2 eta pi^2 t)
#      by(x,y,t) = sin(2 pi x) sin(pi y) exp(-5 eta pi^2 t)
#
#  A single uniform Dirichlet BC set (b = 0 everywhere) is valid for both modes.
#
#  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  HONEST CAVEAT -- read this before quoting this case as physics validation
#  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The initial condition above is NOT divergence-free
#  (div b = d(bx)/dx + d(by)/dy != 0). It is therefore NOT a physically
#  admissible magnetic field. This case validates the MULTI-COMPONENT
#  MACHINERY (component independence, per-component rates, no component swap),
#  not the Gauss law. It is admissible *only* because the solver transports each
#  component independently and never enforces div b = 0 (a documented
#  limitation -- see documentation/classes.md).
#
#  This is not an oversight: in 2D it is impossible to do better here. A
#  divergence-free field that vanishes on the WHOLE boundary must be identically
#  zero (the div-curl identity gives int |grad b|^2 = 0), and if one component
#  varies only in y (so that div b = dbx/dx = 0) the other must be
#  y-independent -- which requires DIFFERENT boundary conditions per component.
#  TRUST scalar CLs apply one uniform condition to all components, so both
#  requirements cannot be met at once.
# =============================================================================

dimension 2
Pb_MHD pb
Domaine dom

# --------------------------------- mesh ------------------------------------
Mailler dom
{
    Pave pavé
    {
        Origine              0.  0.
        Nombre_de_Noeuds     49  49
        Longueurs            1.  1.
    }
    {
        Bord gauche   X = 0.    0. <= Y <= 1.
        Bord droite   X = 1.    0. <= Y <= 1.
        Bord bas      Y = 0.    0. <= X <= 1.
        Bord haut     Y = 1.    0. <= X <= 1.
    }
}

Decouper dom
{
    Partitionneur tranche { tranches 2 2 }
    Larg_joint 2
    Nom_Zones dom
}
Fin

Scatter dom.Zones dom

Polymac_p0 dis

Associate pb dom
Discretize pb dis

# ------------------------------ time integration ----------------------------
#  eta = 0.02, so bx decays as exp(-2*0.02*pi^2*t), by as exp(-5*0.02*pi^2*t)
Schema_euler_implicit sch
Read sch
{
    tinit 0.
    tmax 0.5
    dt_max 0.005
    facsec 1e6
    facsec_max 1e6
    solveur implicite { solveur petsc cli { } }
}

Associate pb sch

# ---------------------------------- physics ---------------------------------
Read pb
{
    fluide_incompressible
    {
        mu      Champ_Uniforme 1 1.0
        rho     Champ_Uniforme 1 1.0
        lambda  Champ_Uniforme 1 1.0
        Cp      Champ_Uniforme 1 1.0
        beta_th Champ_Uniforme 1 0.0
    }

    Convection_Diffusion_Magnetic_field
    {
        # nb_composantes omitted on purpose -> defaults to the dimension (2)
        diffusivite_magnetique Champ_Uniforme 1 0.02
        # no `vitesse_magnetique` -> u = 0, pure diffusion

        diffusion  { }
        convection { amont }

        boundary_conditions
        {
            # homogeneous Dirichlet on all faces (valid for both eigenmodes)
            Bord gauche  Temperature_imposee_paroi Champ_front_uniforme 2 0. 0.
            Bord droite  Temperature_imposee_paroi Champ_front_uniforme 2 0. 0.
            Bord bas     Temperature_imposee_paroi Champ_front_uniforme 2 0. 0.
            Bord haut    Temperature_imposee_paroi Champ_front_uniforme 2 0. 0.
        }
        # component 0 (bx) = sin(pi x)  sin(pi y)  -> rate 2 eta pi^2
        # component 1 (by) = sin(2 pi x) sin(pi y)  -> rate 5 eta pi^2
        initial_conditions
        {
            magnetic_field Champ_Fonc_xyz dom 2 sin(pi*x)*sin(pi*y) sin(2*pi*x)*sin(pi*y)
        }
    }
}

# --------------------------------- postprocessing ---------------------------
#  Probe each component separately (per-component names magnetic_field0/1) at a
#  point where BOTH are non-zero, so a swap would be immediately visible.
Postraitement
{
    Sondes
    {
        # (x=0.25, y=0.5): bx = sin(pi/4)*sin(pi/2)=0.707, by = sin(pi/2)*1=1
        sonde_bx grav magnetic_field0 Periode dts Points 1 0.25 0.5
        sonde_by grav magnetic_field1 Periode dts Points 1 0.25 0.5
    }
}

Solve pb